[0.652, "o", "\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\bbackupctl --init-server"]
[0.735, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[0.002, "o", "[1/10] restic is already installed\r\n[2/10] database dump tools are installed\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "[3/10] creating user backup-user (no password, SSH key only)\r\n"]
[0.034, "o", "[4/10] creating directory /home/backup-user/backups/restic-repo\r\n[4/10] creating directory /home/backup-user/backups/dumps\r\n[5/10] setting root:backup-user 750+setgid permissions on /home/backup-user/backups\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "[6/10] generating a restic password into /root/.restic-env\r\n\r\n⚠ RESTIC PASSWORD (save it separately — this is the only chance to decrypt\r\n  the backups if the server is lost, backupctl will never show it again):\r\n\r\n  elrHV955aUj1OjPjZEpgh5YF2WCVUBV3IsiUc35alcI\r\n\r\nIt has also been written to /root/.restic-env (owned by root, mode 600).\r\n\r\n"]
[0.007, "o", "[7/10] initializing restic repository /home/backup-user/backups/restic-repo\r\n"]
[2.660, "o", "created restic repository 152a186d61 at /home/backup-user/backups/restic-repo\r\n\r\nPlease note that knowledge of your password is required to access\r\nthe repository. Losing your password means that your data is\r\nirrecoverably lost.\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "[8/10] writing /root/backup.sh\r\n[9/10] writing the systemd unit + timer\r\n"]
[0.148, "o", "[10/10] starting restic-backup.timer\r\n"]
[0.013, "o", "Created symlink /etc/systemd/system/timers.target.wants/restic-backup.timer -> /etc/systemd/system/restic-backup.timer.\r\r\n"]
[0.156, "o", "--init-server: done\r\n\r\nWhat's next:\r\n  1. Test a one-off run without waiting for the schedule:\r\n       sudo systemctl start restic-backup.service\r\n       journalctl -u restic-backup.service -n 50 --no-pager\r\n  2. On the client that will pull the backups:\r\n       backupctl --gen-config-client -out=backup-client.yaml -client-remote=`whoami`@<this-server-ip> ...\r\n       backupctl --init-client-systemd -config=backup-client.yaml   # or pm2/launchd/task-scheduler\r\n  3. On this server, allow the client's SSH key (the client will print the\r\n     ready-to-run command in step 2):\r\n       sudo backupctl --add-client-key -pubkey=\"ssh-ed25519 ...\"\r\n\r\nAdded a new database to databases: in backup.yaml? Just run --init-server\r\nagain — it's idempotent and will rewrite backup.sh and the timer, nothing\r\ngets broken.\r\n\r\nDetails: backupctl --info\r\n\u001b]0;root@postgres: /root\u0007\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;33mroot@postgres \u001b[01;34m~\u001b[00m# \u001b[K"]
[22.885, "o", "\u001b[7msystemctl start restic-backup.service\u001b[27m"]
[0.702, "o", "\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\b\bsystemctl start restic-backup.service\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
